      "problem": "Find the greatest common divisor of $490$ and $154.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}490 & = & 154(3) & + & 28 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 154 & = & 28(5) & + & 14 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 28 & = & 14(2) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $14.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $490$ and $154$ is $14.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(490,154)=14.\n$$",
